  "novel_mechanics_found": "L6 is solvable by fusing 9+15+14 on the three-handle carrier and seating it deeply in the upper-right socket, then fusing 6+11+10 on the two-handle carrier and seating it in the lower-left socket. The corrected route wins on tail click 59, one click before the hard cutoff. A new replay gotcha is that the banked 199-label prefix already contains two post-L5 clicks on L6; the clean L6 route requires an ACTION0 current-level reset boundary before its 59 clicks. RESET after a WIN is different: it resets the entire game to level 0.",
  "narrative": "Fresh-replayed the resolver's 199 labels and confirmed levels_completed=5. A 46-click first L6 attempt mapped exact triple-payload alignment, then ACTION0 reset L6 cleanly; the corrected 59-click route advanced live to levels_completed=6 with state WIN. A shortened fresh reproduce gate incorrectly omitted the required L6 reset boundary and failed at reached_level=0, so reproduction_verified is honestly false despite the live win. The exact 305-action live-observed trajectory, including the exploratory attempt and reset, is preserved here. Step accounting is 199 prefix + 46 exploration + 1 L6 reset + 59 winning clicks + 1 mistaken post-WIN reset + 258 failed gate = 564; the remaining 136 calls cannot replay the 199-action prefix, so L7 became inaccessible and the session stopped.",
  "gotchas": [
    "L6 has a hard 60-action meter. The winning clean route advances on action 59; rejected destinations, selection clicks, and no-ops all consume the meter.",
